# The actor rerolls `quantity` of the stored results of `whose`: it rolls the noted kind of die
# for each, unstores the rerolled results and stores the new ones [CR#706.8b]. It is not
# `rollDice` then `storeResults`: `rollDice` names the sides it rolls, while a reroll rolls the
# kind each stored result noted, and nothing else unstores a result.
primitive rerollStored(quantity: Quantity, whose: NounPhrase): Action = RerollStored
